    {
      "id": "card.ancient_egypt.030.c3",
      "type": "text",
      "role": "explain",
      "headline": "Why a pyramid?",
      "body": "Why that shape at all? Egyptologists have a few ideas. The pyramid may have been a stairway for the king’s spirit to climb to the heavens. It may have stood for the mound of creation. Or it may have pictured the sun’s rays reaching down to earth. Each idea points the same way: up."
    },
    {
      "id": "card.ancient_egypt.030.c4",
      "type": "text",
      "role": "explain",
      "headline": "One story",
      "body": "Crews of Egyptians, called up in turns and paid for their work, dragged stone on sledges over wetted sand, fed by bakeries and silos. They raised a pyramid that stayed the tallest human-made structure for about 3,800 years. Then robbers taught the lesson every pyramid had been advertising, and New Kingdom rulers chose hidden tombs."
    },
